Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:17:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(cloud-sync): run scheduled sync in-process instead of
 an unauthenticated self-fetch

The 15-minute cloud sync scheduler called POST /api/sync/cloud on its own
server without credentials. That route requires auth, so once a dashboard
password was set every scheduled sync got a 401 that was swallowed by the
scheduler's catch-all, and automatic sync silently never ran. Manual sync
from the dashboard still worked because it carries a session cookie.

The route's "sync" action only calls syncToCloud(machineId), so the
scheduler now calls it directly. Scheduled-sync failures are logged
instead of discarded. Adds a regression test that fails on the old code.

